      <description>&lt;p&gt;In microstates A, B, C and D, these high-attention edges were mainly concentrated among temporal electrodes and their neighboring sites (around T3–T6), suggesting that MulB-GAT relied on several temporal hub-centered pathways when aggregating neighborhood information. 















